{"id": "c003", "parent": "c002", "source_sha256": "fbdf01cdc822b35085cbcec82cf1d86aee73954a8a7823d0fa9d006f9ad8899f", "hypothesis": "Tiny cases were still ~0.060ms after removing the host sync; the residual fixed cost is the kernel launch plus the two zeros/full init-memset kernels. In the packed ragged layout every output/lse row is fully written by exactly one program per head (zero-length seqs produce no rows), so torch.empty is correct and drops 2 memset launches per call, further cutting tiny-case latency.", "change_from_parent": "allocation only: torch.zeros/torch.full -> torch.empty for output/lse on the main path (empty-batch/max_seqlen==0 guards keep zeros/full since no kernel runs). Kernel body and grid logic byte-identical to c002.", "config": {"BLOCK_M": 128, "BLOCK_N": 64, "num_warps": 8, "num_stages": 2, "grid": "V1-dense; sync-free for total_q<=128", "qk_precision": "bf16-dot-fp32-accum", "launch": "sync-free-small + no-memset (torch.empty)", "host_syncs": "0 for total_q<=128, else 1", "causal_skip": true}, "validation": {"correct": true, "workloads_passed": 21, "workloads_total": 21, "failures": [], "tolerance": {"atol": 0.01, "rtol": 0.01, "matched_ratio": 0.99}}, "per_workload": [{"uuid": "f7a038e9-6c18-4fd6-9b79-e349a4c79bd8", "regime": "tiny", "axes": {"total_q": 7, "len_indptr": 2}, "correct": true, "speedup": 8.00}, {"uuid": "f4c23a33-b16b-4ee8-bb86-440562adf047", "regime": "micro", "axes": {"total_q": 1, "len_indptr": 2}, "correct": true, "speedup": 7.26}, {"uuid": "bad384fa-037d-474f-9a09-0e9f1bb8f43e", "regime": "tiny", "axes": {"total_q": 35, "len_indptr": 2}, "correct": true, "speedup": 8.52}, {"uuid": "2068cdff-fad7-43d3-b018-490349ad9776", "regime": "small", "axes": {"total_q": 81, "len_indptr": 3}, "correct": true, "speedup": 14.57}, {"uuid": "6f3e1bfe-2209-4921-9be4-beed5c9744cb", "regime": "large", "axes": {"total_q": 13557, "len_indptr": 26}, "correct": true, "speedup": 31.54}, {"uuid": "adefedc4-d82a-43ca-800e-51557b08b446", "regime